      "IB Gram works with Canadian families whose children study inside a public school board, an independent school, or a Cambridge/Edexcel IGCSE programme. That is a wide group, because Canada runs the IB unusually close to the mainstream: a large share of the country's IB Diploma students sit inside ordinary public high schools rather than fee-paying academies, earning both the IB Diploma and their provincial credential — the Ontario Secondary School Diploma, the BC Dogwood, Alberta's High School Diploma — in the same two years. All tutoring for Canadian families is delivered online, scheduled to your own time zone. We do not send tutors to homes inside Canada; home tutoring is offered only in India. If your child needs a subject specialist who already knows the exact course they are graded against, that is the match we build.",
